### 1. Get all reservations (expect count 5)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations

### 2. Filter by date (expect count 3)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations?date=2026-10-10

### 3. Available tables for 4 guests on Oct 10, 7 PM (expect count 6)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/availability?date=2026-10-10&time=19:00&guests=4

### 4. Book Table 6 on Oct 10, 7 PM (expect 201: the cancelled booking does NOT block it)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Bea Villanueva",
  "customerEmail": "bea.villanueva@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09271234567",
  "table": "t6",
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4,
  "specialRequest": "Anniversary dinner"
}

### 5. CONFLICT: Table 5 on Oct 10, 7 PM is already Confirmed (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Miguel Torres",
  "customerEmail": "miguel.torres@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09351234567",
  "table": "t5",
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 6. CONFLICT: Table 6 again, now taken by request #4 (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Miguel Torres",
  "customerEmail": "miguel.torres@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09351234567",
  "table": "t6",
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "time": "19:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 7. Same table, DIFFERENT time slot (expect 201: no conflict)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Miguel Torres",
  "customerEmail": "miguel.torres@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09351234567",
  "table": "t5",
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "time": "17:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 8. Too many guests for a 2-seater (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Liza Ramos",
  "customerEmail": "liza.ramos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09061234567",
  "table": "t2",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "13:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 9. Out-of-service table, Table 11 (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Liza Ramos",
  "customerEmail": "liza.ramos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09061234567",
  "table": "t11",
  "date": "2026-10-15",
  "time": "13:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 10. Past date (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Liza Ramos",
  "customerEmail": "liza.ramos@gmail.com",
  "customerPhone": "09061234567",
  "table": "t7",
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "time": "13:00",
  "guests": 4
}

### 11. Many invalid fields (expect 400 with 5 errors)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "",
  "customerEmail": "maria@",
  "customerPhone": "12345",
  "table": "t5",
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "time": "18:30",
  "guests": 0
}

### 12. Availability again (expect count 5: Table 6 is now taken)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/availability?date=2026-10-10&time=19:00&guests=4

### 13. Availability with missing guests (expect 400)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/availability?date=2026-10-10&time=19:00

### 14. One reservation with full table details (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r1

### 15. Reservation that does not exist (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations/r999

### 16. All reservations again (expect count 7: 5 original + #4 + #7)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/reservations
